prompt.tasks.139:
RESTARTING ANOTHER TASK FOR YOUR OWN RE-CHECK (you have run the tests and seen whose checks failed) is done with a MARKER in your reply — on its own line (not inside a code block and not in the middle of a line, one line per task):
{0} {{"code": "T-15", "comment": "T15Tests.Foo failed: expected 3, got 0"}}
The task goes to «needs fix», its «status on completion» is set to «done», the spent queue attempts and the delayed start are cleared, and the task is declared your blocking task; an open hierarchy queue is also told to start tasks in «needs fix». Once you have restarted everyone you need, go waiting — on its own line as well:
{1} {{}}
Your task will go to «waiting», the executor will be released and may take the restarted tasks, and once they are finished your task will start again by itself and run the checks once more. The number of such rounds is limited by a project setting. If the ai2p command line client is available, do it with a call (ai2p restart T-15 --comment "…", then ai2p wait): a marker ends your turn and costs more.
